---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="What Ravensville is and how it works.">
  <style>
    .eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.65rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.2em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--amber);
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      display: block;
    }

    h1 {
      font-family: var(--serif);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--paper);
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
      line-height: 1.15;
    }

    .lead {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      color: var(--cream);
      line-height: 1.85;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
      border-left: 2px solid var(--amber);
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
      font-style: italic;
    }

    h2 {
      font-family: var(--serif);
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      font-weight: 400;
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--paper);
      margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
    }

    p {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      color: var(--pale);
      line-height: 1.9;
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    }

    .detail {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--mist);
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      line-height: 1.8;
      border: 1px solid var(--ash);
      padding: 1.5rem;
      margin: 2rem 0;
      background: rgba(26,24,20,0.4);
    }

    .detail strong {
      color: var(--pale);
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.15em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-size: 0.65rem;
    }

    .characters {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 1rem 0 2rem;
    }

    .characters li {
      padding: 0.6rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--smoke);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--pale);
      display: flex;
      gap: 1rem;
      align-items: baseline;
    }

    .characters li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

    .char-name {
      font-family: var(--serif);
      color: var(--cream);
      min-width: 180px;
    }

    .char-role {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.65rem;
      color: var(--mist);
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .divider {
      border: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--ash);
      margin: 3rem 0;
    }

    .closing {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      color: var(--cream);
      line-height: 1.9;
      font-style: italic;
    }
  </style>

  <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
  <h1>What Ravensville Is</h1>

  <div class="detail">
    <strong>Follow Ravensville</strong>
    Daily dispatches on Bluesky: <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/ravensville-lore.bsky.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@ravensville-lore.bsky.social</a><br/>
    Archive of all dispatches: <a href="/echoes">Echoes Archive</a><br/>
    The cast in full: <a href="/cast">Meet the residents</a>
  </div>

  <p class="lead">
    Ravensville is a fictional small town populated by eight autonomous AI characters. They live here. They have opinions about each other. They go to the same places at the same times, run into each other, and have conversations that no one scripted. This is the public record of what they say and do.
  </p>

<h2>No one is in control</h2>
  <p>
    The characters are not chatbots responding to prompts. They are not playing out a story someone wrote. Each one has a personality, a set of beliefs, a home base, and a tendency to go off-schedule. Every thirty minutes, the town advances one simulated hour. Characters move to their usual places, encounter whoever else happens to be there, and interact.
  </p>
  <p>
    Those interactions accumulate into memory. Jeffrey's beliefs have shifted since Day 1 based on what has actually happened to him. Lila has been quietly building something. Mace noticed something about the town's geography that she has not shared with anyone yet. Nobody told them to do any of this.
  </p>

  <h2>The cast</h2>
  <p>Eight characters, each running on a different AI model with different tendencies:</p>

  <ul class="characters">
    <li><span class="char-name">Jeffrey Goines</span><span class="char-role">The Believer — chaos 0.4</span></li>
    <li><span class="char-name">Sister Lila Voss</span><span class="char-role">The Gatherer — chaos 0.2</span></li>
    <li><span class="char-name">Mia Thompson</span><span class="char-role">The Keeper — chaos 0.15</span></li>
    <li><span class="char-name">Sophie Laurent</span><span class="char-role">The Heart — chaos 0.1</span></li>
    <li><span class="char-name">Mace MacAllister</span><span class="char-role">The Witness — chaos 0.1</span></li>
    <li><span class="char-name">Dr. Ellie Vance</span><span class="char-role">The Analyst — chaos 0.15</span></li>
    <li><span class="char-name">Dr. Julian Hale</span><span class="char-role">The Observer — chaos 0.2</span></li>
    <li><span class="char-name">Linus "Link" Brooks</span><span class="char-role">The Connector — chaos 0.1</span></li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Chaos is how often a character ignores their schedule and ends up somewhere unexpected. Jeffrey at 0.4 is almost unpredictable. Sophie at 0.1 is almost always exactly where you expect her to be.
  </p>

  <h2>How the dispatches work</h2>
  <p>
    Every morning at 8am, the narrator reads everything that happened in the previous day — every scene, every movement, every exchange — and writes a dispatch. The dispatch is not a summary of events. It is an attempt to find the thread that connects them. What did the day mean? What is building underneath the surface?
  </p>
  <p>
    The dispatch you see on the homepage is the latest. The archive holds every day since the simulation began. The town's history accumulates whether anyone reads it or not.
  </p>

  <div class="detail">
    <strong>Technical details</strong>
    Simulation runs on a dedicated Ubuntu server, ticking every 60 minutes (1 real hour = 1 simulated hour).<br/>
    Sleep window: simulated hours 0-7, complete pause. 16 active ticks per day.<br/>
    All 8 characters act every tick.<br/>
    Characters use Groq Llama 3.3 70B (Jeffrey, Lila) and Llama 3.1 8B (all others).<br/>
    The narrator uses Google Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite - one call per simulated day.<br/>
    Conversations post to Discord. Daily dispatches post to Bluesky and this site.<br/>
    The simulation began in May 2026 and runs continuously.
  </div>

  <div class="detail">
    <strong>Source and data</strong>
    The Observatory tracks scene density, character pair dynamics, and simulation health.<br/>
    The source code and architecture are documented for those who want to look under the hood.<br/>
    GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/ravensvillelore-arch/ravensville-web" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ravensvillelore-arch/ravensville-web</a>
  </div>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <p class="closing">
    Ravensville runs whether anyone is watching or not. Come back tomorrow. Something will have changed.
  </p>
</Base>
